# Transaction Ledger API: manual walkthrough
#
# VS Code: install the "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client), start the API with
# `docker compose up --build`, then click "Send Request" above each request, top to bottom.
# Later requests reuse ids from earlier responses, e.g. {{alice.response.body.$.id}}.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000/api/v1

### Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Create account Alice  →  201, balance "0.00"
# @name alice
POST {{baseUrl}}/accounts
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Alice Johnson"}

### Create account Bob
# @name bob
POST {{baseUrl}}/accounts
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Bob Smith"}

### Client cannot set the balance  →  400 VALIDATION_ERROR
POST {{baseUrl}}/accounts
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Mallory", "balance": 1000000}

### Credit Alice 100  →  201, balance_after "100.00"
POST {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{alice.response.body.$.id}}/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{"type": "credit", "amount": "100.00", "reference_id": "deposit-001", "description": "Salary"}

### Same reference again  →  409 DUPLICATE_TRANSACTION, original returned, balance unchanged
POST {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{alice.response.body.$.id}}/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{"type": "credit", "amount": "100.00", "reference_id": "deposit-001"}

### Credit 50 (amount as a JSON number)  →  balance_after "150.00"
POST {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{alice.response.body.$.id}}/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{"type": "credit", "amount": 50, "reference_id": "deposit-002"}

### Debit 30  →  balance_after "120.00"
POST {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{alice.response.body.$.id}}/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{"type": "debit", "amount": "30.00", "reference_id": "withdrawal-001"}

### Overdraft  →  422 INSUFFICIENT_BALANCE, nothing stored
POST {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{alice.response.body.$.id}}/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{"type": "debit", "amount": "1000.00", "reference_id": "withdrawal-002"}

### Debit 20  →  balance_after "100.00"  (spec: 0 +100 +50 -30 -20 = 100)
POST {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{alice.response.body.$.id}}/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{"type": "debit", "amount": "20.00", "reference_id": "withdrawal-003"}

### Balance  →  "100.00"
GET {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{alice.response.body.$.id}}/balance

### Invalid amount (3 decimals)  →  400 INVALID_AMOUNT
POST {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{alice.response.body.$.id}}/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{"type": "credit", "amount": 10.005, "reference_id": "bad-amount"}

### Invalid type  →  400 INVALID_TRANSACTION_TYPE
POST {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{alice.response.body.$.id}}/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{"type": "refund", "amount": "10.00", "reference_id": "bad-type"}

### History: newest first, both types
GET {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{alice.response.body.$.id}}/transactions

### History: debits only, 2 per page
GET {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{alice.response.body.$.id}}/transactions?type=debit&page=1&limit=2

### History: page past the end  →  200, empty data, correct metadata
GET {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{alice.response.body.$.id}}/transactions?page=99

### History: invalid limit  →  400 INVALID_PAGINATION
GET {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{alice.response.body.$.id}}/transactions?limit=500

### Transfer 30 Alice → Bob  →  201, Alice "70.00", Bob "30.00"
POST {{baseUrl}}/transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "from_account_id": "{{alice.response.body.$.id}}",
  "to_account_id": "{{bob.response.body.$.id}}",
  "amount": "30.00",
  "reference_id": "rent-2026-10",
  "description": "October rent"
}

### Same transfer reference again  →  409 DUPLICATE_TRANSFER, no money moved
POST {{baseUrl}}/transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "from_account_id": "{{alice.response.body.$.id}}",
  "to_account_id": "{{bob.response.body.$.id}}",
  "amount": "30.00",
  "reference_id": "rent-2026-10"
}

### Transfer more than the balance  →  422 INSUFFICIENT_BALANCE
POST {{baseUrl}}/transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "from_account_id": "{{alice.response.body.$.id}}",
  "to_account_id": "{{bob.response.body.$.id}}",
  "amount": "5000.00",
  "reference_id": "too-much"
}

### Transfer to the same account  →  400 SAME_ACCOUNT_TRANSFER
POST {{baseUrl}}/transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "from_account_id": "{{alice.response.body.$.id}}",
  "to_account_id": "{{alice.response.body.$.id}}",
  "amount": "1.00",
  "reference_id": "self"
}

### Bob's history shows the transfer's credit leg (reference transfer:<id>:credit)
GET {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{bob.response.body.$.id}}/transactions

### Unknown account  →  404 ACCOUNT_NOT_FOUND
GET {{baseUrl}}/accounts/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### Malformed account id  →  400 INVALID_ACCOUNT_ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/accounts/not-a-uuid

### Transactions cannot be deleted  →  405 METHOD_NOT_ALLOWED (Allow: GET, POST)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{alice.response.body.$.id}}/transactions

### Unknown route  →  404 NOT_FOUND in the standard error format
GET {{baseUrl}}/does-not-exist
